# Python Source Standards

- Respect hexagonal boundaries: no infrastructure imports in domain/application.
- Import ports only from facade: `from bioetl.domain.ports import ...`.
- Domain code must stay pure: no I/O, no HTTP clients, no filesystem operations.
- Dependency injection via constructors; wiring and factories stay in `composition/`.
- Public APIs require explicit type hints and must remain `mypy --strict` friendly.
- Naming: use project suffixes (`*Port`, `*Service`, `*Factory`, `*Adapter`, etc.).
- For Silver layer writes, use Delta Lake contracts; raw non-ACID parquet is forbidden.
- Prefer structured logging ports instead of `print()`.
